[statement]
A POSIX header ending in star's trailer, `tar` and a NUL, with a prefix
of three bytes and star's two times as star writes them, eleven digits
and a space, after another member. Every reader lists the members, as
ferrotape does. Go reports the times as the member's access and change
times, which the catalog does not record.

[archive]
header name=first
data "1\n"
header name=file prefix=dir @476="00000001750 00000003720 " @508="tar\x00"
header name=after
end

[verdict]
all: read

[gnu-tar 1.35]
member listed=- path=first size=2 mode=0o644 data="1\n"
member listed=- path=dir/file size=0 mode=0o644 data=""
member listed=- path=after size=0 mode=0o644 data=""
exit 0

